<h2 id="lti">4. LTI shaping</h2>

<p>
A linear time-invariant filter shapes spectra by multiplication:
</p>

$$
S_&#123;YY&#125;(\omega)=|H(\omega)|^2S_&#123;XX&#125;(\omega).
$$

<p>
The filter ignores the random phases of the input; at the second-order level it
scales each frequency's power.
</p>

<Figure title="Figure 3 · Input PSD, filter gain, and output PSD" canvasId="fig3" width="780" height="360" readoutId="fig3-readout">
<Fragment slot="legend">
  <div class="legend">
      <span><span class="swatch" style="background:#1f4a8c"></span>$S_&#123;XX&#125;$</span>
      <span><span class="swatch" style="background:#2d7a3e"></span>$|H|^2$</span>
      <span><span class="swatch" style="background:#b8412a"></span>$S_&#123;YY&#125;$</span>
    </div>
</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="controls">
  <ControlRange id="fig3-center" label="filter center" valueId="fig3-center-v" min="0" max="2.8" step="0.01" value="0" />
      <ControlRange id="fig3-width" label="filter bandwidth" valueId="fig3-width-v" min="0.12" max="2.4" step="0.01" value="1" />
      <PresetRow>
