        <button data-fig3-filter="band">Band-pass</button>
        <button data-fig3-filter="notch">Notch</button>
      </PresetRow>
</Fragment>
</Figure>

<h2 id="periodogram">5. Periodogram estimates</h2>

<p>
The PSD is an ensemble object, but real data gives you finite records. The
periodogram estimates power by squaring Fourier coefficients from one sample path.
It is noisy: longer records reveal the spectral shape better, but single-frequency
estimates still fluctuate.
</p>

<Figure title="Figure 4 · Periodogram convergence with record length" canvasId="fig4" width="780" height="360" readoutId="fig4-readout">
<Fragment slot="controls">
  <PresetRow>
        <button id="fig4-resample">New realization</button>
      </PresetRow>
</Fragment>
</Figure>

<Figure title="Figure 4b · Welch averaging and window choice" canvasId="fig4-welch" width="780" height="360" readoutId="fig4-welch-readout">
<Fragment slot="legend">
